  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $866M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration recorded 112,895 awards with an average award size of $7.7K. The General Services Administration saw obligations down 97.0% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. The General Services Administration’s FY obligations history shows $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $28.9B in FY26, before the FY27 to date total of $866M. The General Services Administration’s top NAICS categories in FY2027 to date include Computer Systems Design Services at $157M and Engineering Services at $127M. The General Services Administration’s leading vendors in FY2027 to date include BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $77.3M and V2X AEROSPACE LLC at $49.1M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How steep is the year-over-year change for FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration’s obligations fell 97.0% year over year. The General Services Administration obligated $866M in FY2027 to date, compared with prior full-year totals ranging from $20.6B to $28.9B in FY22 through FY26. The General Services Administration’s award count is 112,895 with an average award size of $7.7K, reflecting the current fiscal year to date profile."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which categories and contractors account for most FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest category at $157M and Engineering Services is second at $127M. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC is the top vendor at $77.3M and V2X AEROSPACE LLC is second at $49.1M. The General Services Administration also allocated $80.8M to Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and $54.6M to Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology)."
      }
